es; and asset management products, including pooled funds, institutional portfolios and pension funds. The company was formerly known as Sun Life Financial Services of Canada Inc. and changed its name to Sun Life Financial Inc. in July 2003. Sun Life Financial Inc. was founded in 1871 and is headquartered in Toronto, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin David Strain C.A., CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 32K people. Revenue per employee of $909K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $58K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Sun Life Financial Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $38.3B market cap on $29.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $1.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.74\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_head