edian (29%) by 16pp, so it is a below-average operator in its field.","It captures well under its share of sector profits (0.48x its revenue share).","It accounts for 0.7% of sector revenue and 0.4% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-4.3% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.02 across 514 companies in the universe; the top four hold 20% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 40% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 10% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 18% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 21% and a beta of 0.71, it is more defensive than the market.","About $32.3M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 51% in the 2020 crash, 31% in the 2022 bear market and 78% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $49.77 (margin of safety -39%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 1%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $39.36 to $65.20 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Financial Services peers: P/E 18.0 vs 11.6 and P/FCF 20.7 vs 12.2 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 44% above its 10-year median.","The Street target $64.40 on average, 7% below the price.","The price implies 3.9% annual cash-flow growth, 6pp more than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 8.3% by 12pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.17).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","It earns a 15% return on equity."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 18.7% over 3 years and -1.5% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 31%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 2.8% on average.","Analysts expect 6.9% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 56%.","It returns 6.9% a year to shareholders (3.1% in buybacks and 4.0% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 25 consecutive years, raising it 7.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 32,151 employees, each generates about $909K of revenue, 1.8x the Financial Services median, and revenue has grown 3.6% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $58K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.5M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":29,"head":"Avoid: priced 39% above its fair value of $49.77.","pros":["ROE 15.4% vs cost of equity 8.7%","12-1 month momentum +40%","Returns 6.9% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Composite 13, below the 25 line (gates 4/14)","Trades 39% above fair value of $49.77","Revenue shrank 1.5%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 2/9","P/E 18.0x vs sector 11.6x"],"flags":["Priced 39% above its fair value of $49.77","Its composite score (13) is below 25"],"need":[],"buy_below":42.3,"vc":{"base":49.77,"base_src":"dcf","bear":39.36,"bull":65.2,"alt_median":49.74,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.0009,"dispersion":0.01,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":11.606,"ev_ebitda":10.5935,"pfcf":12.2479,"pb":1.3371,"roic":0.1159,"gross_margin":0.4466,"fcf_margin":0.2518,"div_yield":0.0277}},"mc_quantiles":[33.29,36.87,39.36,41.11,42.72,44.17,45.27,46.81,47.78,48.67,49.84,51.5,52.74,54.11,55.48,57.23,59.98,61.9,65.2,71.26,81.91],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.435,"discount_rate":0.487,"terminal_growth":0.031,"exit_multiple":0.047},"ticker":"SLF","date":"2026-11-20"}